# Finish coding tasks with static checks

Before declaring a coding task complete, run `.github/check.sh` from the repo root and fix every failure it reports.

The script checks formatting (`black --check`), types (`mypy` on `tg`), import order (`isort -c tg/*.py`), and unused imports (`flake8 --select=F401`).

```bash
# From the repository root
.github/check.sh
```

- A clean run (exit code 0) is required before the task is done.
- On failure, fix the reported issues and run the script again. Do not finish while it still fails.
- Skip the script only when the task did not change code (questions, reviews, docs-only discussion).
